    evidence_row(name: "char_at", category: TextOps, external_subject: NoExternalSubject, computation: computes(authority: authority_required(home: "std.host_text char_at (declared 2026-11-01 on tidy-ant-251's F5 ruling); std.primitives char_at_contract prices it; no std.algebra free_monoid template exists and none is used"), inputs: "text: HostText, pos: Nat", result: "Optional<HostText>: the one-code-point host text at CODE-POINT position pos; Absent at or past the end", body: body_at(module_path: "std.host_text", decl_name: "char_at")), refusals: RefusalsTyped, realization: NoNativeRealizationClaim, compiler_query: NotACompilerQuery, conflict: NoMeaningConflict, located: "char_at: std.host_text declares it and std.primitive_projection binds it (primitive_char_at, HostRealizedSeam); the realization surfaces the census joins are the builtin registry row (std.primitives hand roster and builtin_function_registry), the contract row char_at_contract, the emit handler, the runtime body and the interpreter arm. OBSERVED behavior of that runtime body (src/v1/runtime_rust.dag), and what this row's edit moved: the indexing rule is v1_rt::char_at_optional, which answers the typed absence (None at or past the end, None for a negative position), and BOTH spellings that v1 evaluation calls -- the free v1_rt::char_at and the RcStr carrier method -- are thin adapters over it that clamp and unwrap to the EMPTY TEXT, marked CHAR_AT-LEGACY-ADAPTER. Absence carried in band and a position invented are therefore confined to those two adapters, neither of which this declaration admits. Cost: constant on the ASCII path, position-proportional otherwise; char_at_contract says work \"pos\" and carrier-insensitive, which understates the general path (named follow-up).", next: "TWO SEAMS, AND THE SECOND IS THE ONE THAT BITES. (a) The declaration is bound by the CHECKER and not by EVALUATION: on the claim route the interpreter answers a free call's VALUE by spelling -- the free_call.char_at arm of gunbc.v1.v1_interpreter_primitive_surface, reached through lookup_eval_builtin_inner before any body is consulted -- so at 956dc433116f a read one past the end still came back as the builtin's empty text while the call's declared type is Optional<HostText>. The follow-up is therefore NOT a self-call and NOT an interpreter arm for this name: it is dispatching a free call by its RESOLVED declaration target (src/v1/04_lookup.dag resolved_declaration_call_target), with spelling-first dispatch applying only where no declaration was bound. That change's discriminating pair lives in v2.test.claim.char_at_unicode_witness: the withheld assertion at_absent of the read at position 4 of the four-code-point sample (green only with resolved-target dispatch) replaces the executed probe the_out_of_range_read_is_a_present_until_resolved_target_dispatch_lands, which asserts today's wrong answer and therefore goes red the moment the fix lands, so the flip cannot be forgotten. A per-name bridge arm in the std.host_text family (the v4_bridge.host_text_chars shape) was considered and REJECTED on measurement: its admission reads the flat, name-merged item registry, so it would answer every char_at call in any closure containing std.host_text, and three pre-existing modules that import std.host_text and spell char_at -- dag/extdeps/numeric/base16.dag, dag/extdeps/languages/yaml/ingest.dag, dag/gunbc/roadmap/roadmap_auth_routes.dag -- consume a String at those sites today. Both halves are receipted in gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.host_seam_realization_is_keyed_by_primitive_spelling. (b) The empty-text return and the negative clamp are deleted from the rule itself, one level down, and survive only in the two legacy adapters named in located above; deleting the adapters is the cutover, not this row's follow-up, and that cutover also removes the ambient builtin from builtin_function_registry and from the std.primitives hand roster beside it. Until that cutover, TWO MEANINGS share the spelling char_at in DISTINCT scopes -- std.host_text's declared operation and the ambient builtin -- which DESIGN section 3 admits only because the scopes differ, and the cutover named here is what removes the duplicate. The ambient call sites (a git grep of char_at( over .dag measures 184 occurrences, about 150 of them outside std and the tests) switch when the namespace wave takes the name, each converting an Int position through std.checked_arithmetic checked_int_to_nat (dag/std/coercion.dag records it as the sanctioned crossing; an `as Nat` cast over an arbitrary Int is refused by the checker)"),,
